    "narrative": "For the July 31st slate, the **Austin Waves** offense is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (75.22) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.23), who represent our highest-ceiling plays. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a highly favorable park factor (+16%), while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** finds himself in a prime spot against Bryce Elder; the platoon advantage against the right-hander provides a significant 14% boost to his efficiency score. Similarly, **Sam Antonacci** (65.85) is an excellent start against Nick Martinez, as his 19% boost from the opposing pitcher\u2019s skill rating combined with a favorable platoon edge and leadoff spot makes him one of the most reliable contributors in today's lineup.\n\nWe are navigating several risks, specifically with **Kyle Tucker** (54.68) and **Andy Pages** (52.85), both of whom are facing the tough Ranger Suarez. While the raw talent of **Kyle Tucker** usually demands a start, his score is suppressed today by the elite opposing arm (-12% SP skill impact). **Andy Pages** remains in the lineup despite the tough matchup due to his utility in stolen base situations, where his speed profile remains a priority for our roster construction. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.61) remains a core start, though he faces a slight 7% penalty for the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Leahy. \n\nRegarding roster management, the most difficult decision was keeping **Nasim Nunez** (51.74) on the bench. While his switch-hitting ability and park factors were appealing, his projected bottom-of-the-order positioning (-8%) ultimately tipped the scale in favor of our higher-scoring utility options like **Miguel Vargas** (55.80). Because many of these projections are based on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions, owners should monitor official reports closely; any sudden drop to the bottom of the order for players like **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson** would necessitate a re-evaluation of their threshold status before first pitch.",
